    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Fit and proper person considerations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "In having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person for\nthe purposes of this Act, the Digital ID Regulator:\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "In having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person for\nthe purposes of this Act, the Digital ID Regulator:\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5db632f3724f3979836cc462722d52372b5a8c472f0455869031167a7d8639d",
      "skos:note": "Fit and proper person considerations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Fit and proper person considerations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "In having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person for\nthe purposes of this Act, the Digital ID Regulator:\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-12-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity classification",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity is a fit and proper person",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Digital ID Regulator has an obligation to consider this"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "The Digital ID Regulator may, on application, accredit certain\nkinds of entities as accredited attribute service providers,\naccredited identity exchange providers, accredited identity service\nproviders or entities that provide, or propose to provide, services of\na kind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\nAn entity’s accreditation is subject to conditions. Some conditions\nare imposed by the Act and others may be imposed by the Digital\nID Regulator or the Accreditation Rules. Conditions may include\nrestrictions relating to the services an entity is accredited to\nprovide, the manner in which those services must be provided and\nthe kinds of restricted attributes of individuals an entity is\nauthorised to collect or disclose.\nThe conditions imposed by the Digital ID Regulator on an entity’s\naccreditation, and the entity’s accreditation itself, can be varied or\nrevoked. Accreditation can also be suspended.\nThe Minister may give directions to the Digital ID Regulator\nregarding the accreditation of an entity if, for reasons of security,\nthe Minister considers it appropriate to do so. The Digital ID\nRegulator must comply with such directions.\nAn accredited entity must deactivate a digital ID of an individual if\nrequested to do so, and must comply with requirements relating to\nthe accessibility and useability of accredited services.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "skos:definition": "The Digital ID Regulator may, on application, accredit certain\nkinds of entities as accredited attribute service providers,\naccredited identity exchange providers, accredited identity service\nproviders or entities that provide, or propose to provide, services of\na kind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\nAn entity’s accreditation is subject to conditions. Some conditions\nare imposed by the Act and others may be imposed by the Digital\nID Regulator or the Accreditation Rules. Conditions may include\nrestrictions relating to the services an entity is accredited to\nprovide, the manner in which those services must be provided and\nthe kinds of restricted attributes of individuals an entity is\nauthorised to collect or disclose.\nThe conditions imposed by the Digital ID Regulator on an entity’s\naccreditation, and the entity’s accreditation itself, can be varied or\nrevoked. Accreditation can also be suspended.\nThe Minister may give directions to the Digital ID Regulator\nregarding the accreditation of an entity if, for reasons of security,\nthe Minister considers it appropriate to do so. The Digital ID\nRegulator must comply with such directions.\nAn accredited entity must deactivate a digital ID of an individual if\nrequested to do so, and must comply with requirements relating to\nthe accessibility and useability of accredited services.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f51a9ae702625e26877484b9678106d24a01ef0883e3bf7801a5a4530ef644cb",
      "skos:note": "An entity must comply with conditions imposed by the Digital ID Regulator on its accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "The Digital ID Regulator may, on application, accredit certain\nkinds of entities as accredited attribute service providers,\naccredited identity exchange providers, accredited identity service\nproviders or entities that provide, or propose to provide, services of\na kind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\nAn entity’s accreditation is subject to conditions. Some conditions\nare imposed by the Act and others may be imposed by the Digital\nID Regulator or the Accreditation Rules. Conditions may include\nrestrictions relating to the services an entity is accredited to\nprovide, the manner in which those services must be provided and\nthe kinds of restricted attributes of individuals an entity is\nauthorised to collect or disclose.\nThe conditions imposed by the Digital ID Regulator on an entity’s\naccreditation, and the entity’s accreditation itself, can be varied or\nrevoked. Accreditation can also be suspended.\nThe Minister may give directions to the Digital ID Regulator\nregarding the accreditation of an entity if, for reasons of security,\nthe Minister considers it appropriate to do so. The Digital ID\nRegulator must comply with such directions.\nAn accredited entity must deactivate a digital ID of an individual if\nrequested to do so, and must comply with requirements relating to\nthe accessibility and useability of accredited services.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-13-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity must comply with conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Application for accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the Digital ID\nRegulator for accreditation as one or more of the following kinds\nof accredited entities:\n(a) an accredited attribute service provider;\n(b) an accredited identity exchange provider;\n(c) an accredited identity service provider;\n(d) an entity that provides, or proposes to provide, a service of a\nkind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\n(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the Digital ID\nRegulator for accreditation as one or more of the following kinds\nof accredited entities:\n(a) an accredited attribute service provider;\n(b) an accredited identity exchange provider;\n(c) an accredited identity service provider;\n(d) an entity that provides, or proposes to provide, a service of a\nkind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\n(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af4af3353f498230a9461ce37c850bd9d0e0edcfe481830a581680fcc5968ff1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Application for accreditation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the Digital ID\nRegulator for accreditation as one or more of the following kinds\nof accredited entities:\n(a) an accredited attribute service provider;\n(b) an accredited identity exchange provider;\n(c) an accredited identity service provider;\n(d) an entity that provides, or proposes to provide, a service of a\nkind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules.\n(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-1",
