    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14(2) Application for accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-14-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4623120c8c72b02822e5c9124f2061d2ee77c55c5784f5fce7e7b8fa58ca10ea",
      "skos:note": "List of entities covered by this section"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-14-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14(2) Application for accreditation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An entity is covered by this section if the entity is one of the\nfollowing:\n(a) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or a State or Territory;\n(b) a registered foreign company within the meaning of the\nCorporations Act 2001;\n(c) a Commonwealth entity, or a Commonwealth company,\nwithin the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013;\n(d) a person or body that is an agency within the meaning of the\nFreedom of Information Act 1982;\n(e) a body specified, or the person holding an office specified, in\nPart I of Schedule 2 to the Freedom of Information Act 1982;\n(f) a department or authority of a State;\n(g) a department or authority of a Territory.\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nAccreditation  Division 2\nSection 15\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-14-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Digital ID Regulator must decide whether to accredit an entity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an entity has made an application under\nsection 14 for accreditation as an accredited entity.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator must decide:\n(a) to accredit the entity; or\n(b) to refuse to accredit the entity.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity:\n(a) as an accredited attribute service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of attribute service provider; or\n(b) as an accredited identity exchange provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity exchange provider; or\n(c) as an accredited identity service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity service provider; or\n(d) if Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of\nparagraph 14(1)(d) prescribe services—as an entity that\nprovides services of the kind prescribed unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services of that\nkind.\n(4) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity if:\n(a) a direction under subsection 27(1) (about security) directing\nthe Digital ID Regulator to refuse to accredit the entity is in\nforce; or\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator is not satisfied that the entity is able\nto comply with this Act; or\n(c) Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of section 28\nrequire specified criteria to be met and the entity does not\nmeet the criteria; or\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an entity has made an application under\nsection 14 for accreditation as an accredited entity.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator must decide:\n(a) to accredit the entity; or\n(b) to refuse to accredit the entity.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity:\n(a) as an accredited attribute service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of attribute service provider; or\n(b) as an accredited identity exchange provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity exchange provider; or\n(c) as an accredited identity service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity service provider; or\n(d) if Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of\nparagraph 14(1)(d) prescribe services—as an entity that\nprovides services of the kind prescribed unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services of that\nkind.\n(4) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity if:\n(a) a direction under subsection 27(1) (about security) directing\nthe Digital ID Regulator to refuse to accredit the entity is in\nforce; or\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator is not satisfied that the entity is able\nto comply with this Act; or\n(c) Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of section 28\nrequire specified criteria to be met and the entity does not\nmeet the criteria; or\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-15-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-15-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-15-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "479456c535a4feff0cfcfd0606bb9fc77f5a0251e8855d175516fa47e75ebfdb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Digital ID Regulator must decide whether to accredit an entity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an entity has made an application under\nsection 14 for accreditation as an accredited entity.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator must decide:\n(a) to accredit the entity; or\n(b) to refuse to accredit the entity.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity:\n(a) as an accredited attribute service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of attribute service provider; or\n(b) as an accredited identity exchange provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity exchange provider; or\n(c) as an accredited identity service provider unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services\ndescribed in the definition of identity service provider; or\n(d) if Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of\nparagraph 14(1)(d) prescribe services—as an entity that\nprovides services of the kind prescribed unless the entity\nprovides, or will provide, some or all of the services of that\nkind.\n(4) The Digital ID Regulator must not accredit an entity if:\n(a) a direction under subsection 27(1) (about security) directing\nthe Digital ID Regulator to refuse to accredit the entity is in\nforce; or\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator is not satisfied that the entity is able\nto comply with this Act; or\n(c) Accreditation Rules made for the purposes of section 28\nrequire specified criteria to be met and the entity does not\nmeet the criteria; or\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation"
    },
