    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Minister’s directions regarding accreditation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to accredit an entity;\n(b) impose conditions on the accreditation of an entity;\n(c) suspend the accreditation of an accredited entity;\n(d) revoke the accreditation of an accredited entity.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the accreditation of an accredited entity cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to accredit an entity;\n(b) impose conditions on the accreditation of an entity;\n(c) suspend the accreditation of an accredited entity;\n(d) revoke the accreditation of an accredited entity.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the accreditation of an accredited entity cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-27-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26fc4fe9206950d5f190bb3d05c6aa82152c430bdb18ce19d1cb3fa7b774d11c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27 Minister’s directions regarding accreditation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to accredit an entity;\n(b) impose conditions on the accreditation of an entity;\n(c) suspend the accreditation of an accredited entity;\n(d) revoke the accreditation of an accredited entity.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the accreditation of an accredited entity cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 2  Accreditation"
    },
