    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Digital IDs must be deactivated on request",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an accredited identity service provider\ngenerates a digital ID of an individual.\n(2) The accredited identity service provider must, if requested to do so\nby the individual, deactivate the digital ID of the individual as soon\nas practicable after receiving the request.\n(3) If a digital ID of an individual is deactivated under subsection (2),\nthe digital ID of the individual:\n(a) must not be used by the accredited identity service provider\nfor verifying the identity of the individual or authenticating a\ndigital ID of the individual; and\n(b) if it can be reactivated, must not be reactivated by the\naccredited identity service provider without the express\nconsent of the individual.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an accredited identity service provider\ngenerates a digital ID of an individual.\n(2) The accredited identity service provider must, if requested to do so\nby the individual, deactivate the digital ID of the individual as soon\nas practicable after receiving the request.\n(3) If a digital ID of an individual is deactivated under subsection (2),\nthe digital ID of the individual:\n(a) must not be used by the accredited identity service provider\nfor verifying the identity of the individual or authenticating a\ndigital ID of the individual; and\n(b) if it can be reactivated, must not be reactivated by the\naccredited identity service provider without the express\nconsent of the individual.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f0b6f3d2929b44227b0d40c234737b4d332ada7c2c7a4e96576dda36aada652"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Digital IDs must be deactivated on request",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an accredited identity service provider\ngenerates a digital ID of an individual.\n(2) The accredited identity service provider must, if requested to do so\nby the individual, deactivate the digital ID of the individual as soon\nas practicable after receiving the request.\n(3) If a digital ID of an individual is deactivated under subsection (2),\nthe digital ID of the individual:\n(a) must not be used by the accredited identity service provider\nfor verifying the identity of the individual or authenticating a\ndigital ID of the individual; and\n(b) if it can be reactivated, must not be reactivated by the\naccredited identity service provider without the express\nconsent of the individual."
    },
