    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Accredited services must be accessible and inclusive",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-30-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1AA) An accredited entity must take reasonable steps to ensure that its\naccredited services are accessible for individuals who experience\nbarriers when creating or using a digital ID.\n(1) The Accreditation Rules must provide for and in relation to\nrequirements relating to the accessibility and useability of the\naccredited services of accredited entities.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID.",
      "skos:definition": "(1AA) An accredited entity must take reasonable steps to ensure that its\naccredited services are accessible for individuals who experience\nbarriers when creating or using a digital ID.\n(1) The Accreditation Rules must provide for and in relation to\nrequirements relating to the accessibility and useability of the\naccredited services of accredited entities.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "95d8e4822b2f627252bef31b984d7206d5e79917fb63367376206fbe1c4cd346"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-30-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Accredited services must be accessible and inclusive",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1AA) An accredited entity must take reasonable steps to ensure that its\naccredited services are accessible for individuals who experience\nbarriers when creating or using a digital ID.\n(1) The Accreditation Rules must provide for and in relation to\nrequirements relating to the accessibility and useability of the\naccredited services of accredited entities.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID."
    },
