        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-30-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2c1c9478ef9637e6ca825e7736940736e46ec70e9a4890f34c9e59fe6050ef0d",
      "skos:note": "Accredited entities must comply with accessibility standards and guidelines.",
      "dc:description": "Compliance with accessibility standards and guidelines"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-30-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30(2) Accredited services must be accessible and inclusive",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Accreditation Rules must:\n(a) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to comply with specified accessibility standards; and\n(b) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to have regard to specified accessibility guidelines;\nand\n\nAccreditation  Chapter 2\nAccreditation  Part 2\nOther matters relating to accreditation  Division 6\nSection 31\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(c) require accredited entities, or specified kinds of accredited\nentities, to conduct useability testing with a diverse range of\nindividuals, covering diversity in disability, age, gender and\nethnicity; and\n(d) specify requirements relating to device or browser access;\nand\n(e) specify requirements relating to the provision of support or\nassistance for individuals who may experience barriers when\ncreating or using a digital ID."
    },
