    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 APP-equivalent agreements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into an\nagreement (an APP-equivalent agreement) with an entity covered\nby subsection (2) that prohibits the entity from collecting, holding,\nusing or disclosing personal information in any way that would, if\nthe entity were an organisation within the meaning of the Privacy\nAct 1988, breach an Australian Privacy Principle.\n(2) The entities are as follows:\n(a) a department or authority of a State;\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nSection 34\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) a department or authority of a Territory.\n(3) The Minister must provide the Information Commissioner with a\ncopy of an APP-equivalent agreement within 14 days after it is\nentered into.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into an\nagreement (an APP-equivalent agreement) with an entity covered\nby subsection (2) that prohibits the entity from collecting, holding,\nusing or disclosing personal information in any way that would, if\nthe entity were an organisation within the meaning of the Privacy\nAct 1988, breach an Australian Privacy Principle.\n(2) The entities are as follows:\n(a) a department or authority of a State;\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nSection 34\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) a department or authority of a Territory.\n(3) The Minister must provide the Information Commissioner with a\ncopy of an APP-equivalent agreement within 14 days after it is\nentered into.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-34-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-34-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-34-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "196dfc96c11d19e88abec5e101271dd65a07460134941781213ec4df816a9f6e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 APP-equivalent agreements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into an\nagreement (an APP-equivalent agreement) with an entity covered\nby subsection (2) that prohibits the entity from collecting, holding,\nusing or disclosing personal information in any way that would, if\nthe entity were an organisation within the meaning of the Privacy\nAct 1988, breach an Australian Privacy Principle.\n(2) The entities are as follows:\n(a) a department or authority of a State;\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nSection 34\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) a department or authority of a Territory.\n(3) The Minister must provide the Information Commissioner with a\ncopy of an APP-equivalent agreement within 14 days after it is\nentered into.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy"
    },
