    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39 Notification of eligible data breaches—accredited entities that are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "APP entities\n(1) This section applies to an accredited entity if the entity:\n(a) is an APP entity; and\n(b) is aware that there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nthere has been an eligible data breach (within the meaning of\nthe Privacy Act 1988) of the entity relating to the entity’s\naccredited services; and\n(c) is required under section 26WK of the Privacy Act 1988 to\ngive the Information Commissioner a statement that complies\nwith subsection 26WK(3) of that Act.\n(2) The entity must also give a copy of the statement to the Digital ID\nRegulator at the same time as the statement is given to the\nInformation Commissioner.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "skos:definition": "APP entities\n(1) This section applies to an accredited entity if the entity:\n(a) is an APP entity; and\n(b) is aware that there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nthere has been an eligible data breach (within the meaning of\nthe Privacy Act 1988) of the entity relating to the entity’s\naccredited services; and\n(c) is required under section 26WK of the Privacy Act 1988 to\ngive the Information Commissioner a statement that complies\nwith subsection 26WK(3) of that Act.\n(2) The entity must also give a copy of the statement to the Digital ID\nRegulator at the same time as the statement is given to the\nInformation Commissioner.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da21d49656d1602e5e09893db949b16f2ee92365403929da218d04409596b348"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39 Notification of eligible data breaches—accredited entities that are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "APP entities\n(1) This section applies to an accredited entity if the entity:\n(a) is an APP entity; and\n(b) is aware that there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nthere has been an eligible data breach (within the meaning of\nthe Privacy Act 1988) of the entity relating to the entity’s\naccredited services; and\n(c) is required under section 26WK of the Privacy Act 1988 to\ngive the Information Commissioner a statement that complies\nwith subsection 26WK(3) of that Act.\n(2) The entity must also give a copy of the statement to the Digital ID\nRegulator at the same time as the statement is given to the\nInformation Commissioner.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39(1) Notification of eligible data breaches—accredited entities that are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-39-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to an accredited entity if the entity:\n(a) is an APP entity; and\n(b) is aware that there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nthere has been an eligible data breach (within the meaning of\nthe Privacy Act 1988) of the entity relating to the entity’s\naccredited services; and\n(c) is required under section 26WK of the Privacy Act 1988 to\ngive the Information Commissioner a statement that complies\nwith subsection 26WK(3) of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to an accredited entity if the entity:\n(a) is an APP entity; and\n(b) is aware that there are reasonable grounds to believe that\nthere has been an eligible data breach (within the meaning of\nthe Privacy Act 1988) of the entity relating to the entity’s\naccredited services; and\n(c) is required under section 26WK of the Privacy Act 1988 to\ngive the Information Commissioner a statement that complies\nwith subsection 26WK(3) of that Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-39-ss-1-norm"
