      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The accredited entity to whom the unique identifier is disclosed must not disclose the unique identifier to any other entity.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The restriction limits the knowledge of the accredited entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(4) Restricting disclosure of unique identifiers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-47-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not apply if the disclosure of the unique\nidentifier is for one or more of the following purposes:\n(a) detecting, reporting or investigating a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a provision of this Act;\n(b) conducting proceedings in relation to a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a civil penalty provision of this Act;\n(c) detecting, reporting or investigating either of the following\nwithin a digital ID system:\n(i) a digital ID fraud incident;\n(ii) a cyber security incident:\n(d) conducting an assessment of the matter referred to in\nparagraph 33C(1)(g) of the Privacy Act 1988 (about\nassessments by the Information Commissioner in relation to\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 48\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nthe handling and maintenance of personal information in\naccordance with certain aspects of this Act);\n(e) detecting, reporting, investigating or prosecuting an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not apply if the disclosure of the unique\nidentifier is for one or more of the following purposes:\n(a) detecting, reporting or investigating a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a provision of this Act;\n(b) conducting proceedings in relation to a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a civil penalty provision of this Act;\n(c) detecting, reporting or investigating either of the following\nwithin a digital ID system:\n(i) a digital ID fraud incident;\n(ii) a cyber security incident:\n(d) conducting an assessment of the matter referred to in\nparagraph 33C(1)(g) of the Privacy Act 1988 (about\nassessments by the Information Commissioner in relation to\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 48\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nthe handling and maintenance of personal information in\naccordance with certain aspects of this Act);\n(e) detecting, reporting, investigating or prosecuting an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51e108aa82f76d975774c682f45261b54c73eb83f5de4621bb0d5f8d23cde2ff",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of unique identifiers is permitted for specific purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-47-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(4) Restricting disclosure of unique identifiers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not apply if the disclosure of the unique\nidentifier is for one or more of the following purposes:\n(a) detecting, reporting or investigating a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a provision of this Act;\n(b) conducting proceedings in relation to a contravention, or an\nalleged contravention, of a civil penalty provision of this Act;\n(c) detecting, reporting or investigating either of the following\nwithin a digital ID system:\n(i) a digital ID fraud incident;\n(ii) a cyber security incident:\n(d) conducting an assessment of the matter referred to in\nparagraph 33C(1)(g) of the Privacy Act 1988 (about\nassessments by the Information Commissioner in relation to\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 48\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nthe handling and maintenance of personal information in\naccordance with certain aspects of this Act);\n(e) detecting, reporting, investigating or prosecuting an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-4"
