    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(5) Restricting disclosure of unique identifiers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-47-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsections (2) and (3) also do not apply if the disclosure of the\nunique identifier is:\n(a) to a contractor engaged by the accredited entity; and\n(b) for the purposes of the contractor providing an accredited\nservice, or part of an accredited service, of the accredited\nentity.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Subsections (2) and (3) also do not apply if the disclosure of the\nunique identifier is:\n(a) to a contractor engaged by the accredited entity; and\n(b) for the purposes of the contractor providing an accredited\nservice, or part of an accredited service, of the accredited\nentity.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-47-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8f122265b1d0a5b5c06e915c5130421d1c88aaa372465f6e79fdc43f13c378e",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of unique identifiers is permitted for contractors engaged by the accredited entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-47-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(5) Restricting disclosure of unique identifiers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsections (2) and (3) also do not apply if the disclosure of the\nunique identifier is:\n(a) to a contractor engaged by the accredited entity; and\n(b) for the purposes of the contractor providing an accredited\nservice, or part of an accredited service, of the accredited\nentity.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)."
    },
