    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Restrictions on collecting, using and disclosing biometric",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "information\n(1) An accredited entity may collect, use or disclose biometric\ninformation of an individual only if:\n(a) the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nsection 49 or 50; and\n(b) unless the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nparagraph 49(3)(a) or subsection 49(5), (6) or (8)—the\nindividual to whom the information relates has expressly\nconsented to the collection, use or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "skos:definition": "information\n(1) An accredited entity may collect, use or disclose biometric\ninformation of an individual only if:\n(a) the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nsection 49 or 50; and\n(b) unless the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nparagraph 49(3)(a) or subsection 49(5), (6) or (8)—the\nindividual to whom the information relates has expressly\nconsented to the collection, use or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a540f6b2c8aba2096ae524ce8507fdc321b81c20491bcc01c047b022359f6b6",
      "skos:note": "Authorized entities must obtain consent before collecting, using or disclosing biometric information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Restrictions on collecting, using and disclosing biometric",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "information\n(1) An accredited entity may collect, use or disclose biometric\ninformation of an individual only if:\n(a) the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nsection 49 or 50; and\n(b) unless the collection, use or disclosure is authorised under\nparagraph 49(3)(a) or subsection 49(5), (6) or (8)—the\nindividual to whom the information relates has expressly\nconsented to the collection, use or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation.\n\nChapter 3  Privacy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-48-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorized entities must obtain consent.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 49 or 50 authorization",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Individual consent required."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49 Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-49"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "information of individuals—general rules\n(1) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n(a) the accredited entity’s conditions on accreditation authorise\nthe collection, use, or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation; and\n(b) the biometric information of the individual is collected, used\nor disclosed for the purposes of the accredited entity doing\neither or both of the following:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual;\n(ii) authenticating the individual to their digital ID.\n(2) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 49\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(a) the biometric information is contained in a verifiable\ncredential that is in the individual’s control; and\n(b) the Accreditation Rules prescribe requirements relating to the\ncollection, use or disclosure of the biometric information;\nand\n(c) the collection, use or disclosure complies with those\nrequirements.\n(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite:\n(a) any law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(whether enacted or made before or after this subsection); or\n(b) a warrant (other than a warrant of a kind mentioned in\nparagraph (3)(a)), authorisation or order issued under such a\nlaw.\n(5) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual if the disclosure is to the individual to whom the\nbiometric information relates.\n(6) An accredited entity is authorised to retain, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n(a) the accredited entity collected the information in accordance\nwith subsection (1); and\n(b) the information is retained, used or disclosed for the purposes\nof undertaking testing in relation to the information; and\n\nChapter 3  Privacy",
      "skos:definition": "information of individuals—general rules\n(1) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n(a) the accredited entity’s conditions on accreditation authorise\nthe collection, use, or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation; and\n(b) the biometric information of the individual is collected, used\nor disclosed for the purposes of the accredited entity doing\neither or both of the following:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual;\n(ii) authenticating the individual to their digital ID.\n(2) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 49\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(a) the biometric information is contained in a verifiable\ncredential that is in the individual’s control; and\n(b) the Accreditation Rules prescribe requirements relating to the\ncollection, use or disclosure of the biometric information;\nand\n(c) the collection, use or disclosure complies with those\nrequirements.\n(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite:\n(a) any law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(whether enacted or made before or after this subsection); or\n(b) a warrant (other than a warrant of a kind mentioned in\nparagraph (3)(a)), authorisation or order issued under such",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a16e3bfe1a6975618475e7571321b337d2ec9f73fb21d16ca74eab9bffc2296"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-49",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49 Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "information of individuals—general rules\n(1) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n(a) the accredited entity’s conditions on accreditation authorise\nthe collection, use, or disclosure of the biometric\ninformation; and\n(b) the biometric information of the individual is collected, used\nor disclosed for the purposes of the accredited entity doing\neither or both of the following:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual;\n(ii) authenticating the individual to their digital ID.\n(2) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n\nPrivacy  Chapter 3\nPrivacy  Part 2\nAdditional privacy safeguards  Division 2\nSection 49\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(a) the biometric information is contained in a verifiable\ncredential that is in the individual’s control; and\n(b) the Accreditation Rules prescribe requirements relating to the\ncollection, use or disclosure of the biometric information;\nand\n(c) the collection, use or disclosure complies with those\nrequirements.\n(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.\n(4) Subsection (3) applies despite:\n(a) any law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(whether enacted or made before or after this subsection); or\n(b) a warrant (other than a warrant of a kind mentioned in\nparagraph (3)(a)), authorisation or order issued under such a\nlaw.\n(5) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual if the disclosure is to the individual to whom the\nbiometric information relates.\n(6) An accredited entity is authorised to retain, use or disclose\nbiometric information of an individual if:\n(a) the accredited entity collected the information in accordance\nwith subsection (1); and\n(b) the information is retained, used or disclosed for the purposes\nof undertaking testing in relation to the information; and\n\nChapter 3  Privacy"
    },
