    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49(3) Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-49-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5abce120c9978f6eb6cc7bac1ee07517f872a5e8e18b704973040065bb239051",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of biometric information is permitted to law enforcement agencies under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-49-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49(3) Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information\nof an individual to a law enforcement agency only if:\n(a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by\nor under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth,\na State or a Territory; or\n(b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the\nindividual to whom the biometric information relates, or\npurports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of:\n(i) verifying the identity of the individual; or\n(ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory."
    },
    {
