    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Personal information must not be used or disclosed for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "prohibited marketing purposes\n(1) An accredited entity must not use or disclose personal information\nabout an individual that is in the entity’s possession or control for\nany of the following purposes:\n(a) offering to supply goods or services;\n(b) advertising or promoting goods or services;\n(c) enabling another entity to offer to supply goods or services;\n(d) enabling another entity to advertise or promote goods or\nservices;\n(e) market research.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure of personal\ninformation about an individual if:\n(a) the information is disclosed to an individual for the purposes\nof:\n(i) offering to supply the entity’s accredited services; or\n(ii) advertising or promoting the entity’s accredited\nservices; and\n(b) the information is disclosed to the individual with the\nindividual’s express consent.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "skos:definition": "prohibited marketing purposes\n(1) An accredited entity must not use or disclose personal information\nabout an individual that is in the entity’s possession or control for\nany of the following purposes:\n(a) offering to supply goods or services;\n(b) advertising or promoting goods or services;\n(c) enabling another entity to offer to supply goods or services;\n(d) enabling another entity to advertise or promote goods or\nservices;\n(e) market research.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure of personal\ninformation about an individual if:\n(a) the information is disclosed to an individual for the purposes\nof:\n(i) offering to supply the entity’s accredited services; or\n(ii) advertising or promoting the entity’s accredited\nservices; and\n(b) the information is disclosed to the individual with the\nindividual’s express consent.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-55-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-55-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "364f80d51b40433d9e2988a50d9599313c45e5e53cc99a28042641ea4b614d3c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Personal information must not be used or disclosed for",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "prohibited marketing purposes\n(1) An accredited entity must not use or disclose personal information\nabout an individual that is in the entity’s possession or control for\nany of the following purposes:\n(a) offering to supply goods or services;\n(b) advertising or promoting goods or services;\n(c) enabling another entity to offer to supply goods or services;\n(d) enabling another entity to advertise or promote goods or\nservices;\n(e) market research.\nCivil penalty:\n1,500 penalty units.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure of personal\ninformation about an individual if:\n(a) the information is disclosed to an individual for the purposes\nof:\n(i) offering to supply the entity’s accredited services; or\n(ii) advertising or promoting the entity’s accredited\nservices; and\n(b) the information is disclosed to the individual with the\nindividual’s express consent.\nNote:\nA person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see\nsection 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)."
    },
