      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity must hold an approval under section 62 to participate in the system.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Attribute service provider is mentioned in column 1 of the table.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Entity must be an accredited attribute service provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Phasing-in of participation in the Australian Government Digital",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "ID System\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine the entities\nthat may apply to the Digital ID Regulator for approval to\nparticipate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.\nNote:\nThe determination may specify entities by class (see\nsubsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n(2) The determination may specify entities in any way, including by\nreference to:\n(a) whether the entities are relying parties or accredited entities;\nor\n(b) kinds of relying parties; or\n(c) kinds of accredited entities; or\n(d) whether the entity belongs to the public or private sector.\n(3) The Minister:\n(a) must not revoke the determination; and\n(b) may vary the determination only to:\n(i) specify additional kinds of entities that may apply; or\n(ii) correct an error, defect or irregularity in the\ndetermination.",
      "skos:definition": "ID System\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine the entities\nthat may apply to the Digital ID Regulator for approval to\nparticipate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.\nNote:\nThe determination may specify entities by class (see\nsubsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n(2) The determination may specify entities in any way, including by\nreference to:\n(a) whether the entities are relying parties or accredited entities;\nor\n(b) kinds of relying parties; or\n(c) kinds of accredited entities; or\n(d) whether the entity belongs to the public or private sector.\n(3) The Minister:\n(a) must not revoke the determination; and\n(b) may vary the determination only to:\n(i) specify additional kinds of entities that may apply; or\n(ii) correct an error, defect or irregularity in the\ndetermination.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-60-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-60-ss-2"
