    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63 Approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-63"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "System is subject to conditions\n(1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is subject to the following\nconditions (the approval conditions):\n(a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1);\n(b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 64(2), including as varied under\nsubsection 66(1);\n(c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for\nthe purposes of subsection 64(5).\n(2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System must comply with the approval\nconditions that apply to the entity.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 64\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote:\nFailure to comply with an approval condition may result in a\nsuspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see\nsections 71 and 72).",
      "skos:definition": "System is subject to conditions\n(1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is subject to the following\nconditions (the approval conditions):\n(a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1);\n(b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 64(2), including as varied under\nsubsection 66(1);\n(c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for\nthe purposes of subsection 64(5).\n(2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System must comply with the approval\nconditions that apply to the entity.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 64\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote:\nFailure to comply with an approval condition may result in a\nsuspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see\nsections 71 and 72).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8cee048ade5b818576207fdb12e87c1b65890890396860a71ae00db88833d23"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "System is subject to conditions\n(1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is subject to the following\nconditions (the approval conditions):\n(a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1);\n(b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 64(2), including as varied under\nsubsection 66(1);\n(c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for\nthe purposes of subsection 64(5).\n(2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System must comply with the approval\nconditions that apply to the entity.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 64\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote:\nFailure to comply with an approval condition may result in a\nsuspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see\nsections 71 and 72)."
    },
