    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66 Variation and revocation of conditions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator may vary or revoke a condition imposed\non an entity’s approval under paragraph 64(2)(a):\n(a) at any time, on the Digital ID Regulator’s own initiative; or\n(b) on application by the entity under section 67;\nif the Digital ID Regulator considers it is appropriate to do so.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Digital ID Regulator may have\nregard to matters relating to the security, reliability and stability of\nthe Australian Government Digital ID System when considering\nwhether it is appropriate to vary or revoke a condition.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must revoke a condition imposed under\nparagraph 64(2)(b) if the direction to impose the condition is\nrevoked.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator may vary or revoke a condition imposed\non an entity’s approval under paragraph 64(2)(a):\n(a) at any time, on the Digital ID Regulator’s own initiative; or\n(b) on application by the entity under section 67;\nif the Digital ID Regulator considers it is appropriate to do so.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Digital ID Regulator may have\nregard to matters relating to the security, reliability and stability of\nthe Australian Government Digital ID System when considering\nwhether it is appropriate to vary or revoke a condition.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must revoke a condition imposed under\nparagraph 64(2)(b) if the direction to impose the condition is\nrevoked.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-66-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-66-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-66-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "533acf918f7141e2c506af689400d3fdb41c24541351782eacc99bb60cde3ff9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66 Variation and revocation of conditions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator may vary or revoke a condition imposed\non an entity’s approval under paragraph 64(2)(a):\n(a) at any time, on the Digital ID Regulator’s own initiative; or\n(b) on application by the entity under section 67;\nif the Digital ID Regulator considers it is appropriate to do so.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Digital ID Regulator may have\nregard to matters relating to the security, reliability and stability of\nthe Australian Government Digital ID System when considering\nwhether it is appropriate to vary or revoke a condition.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must revoke a condition imposed under\nparagraph 64(2)(b) if the direction to impose the condition is\nrevoked."
    },
