    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67 Applying for variation or revocation of conditions on approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-67"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System may apply for a condition imposed\non the approval under paragraph 64(2)(a) to be varied or revoked.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System may apply for a condition imposed\non the approval under paragraph 64(2)(a) to be varied or revoked.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bd3a427a1faddb8335b4f589fc2e82f23c560e4bbdf2762b318cb9faa366ce7c",
      "skos:note": "May apply for variation or revocation of conditions on approval"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-67",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67 Applying for variation or revocation of conditions on approval",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System may apply for a condition imposed\non the approval under paragraph 64(2)(a) to be varied or revoked.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-67-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Can",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Entity can apply for variation or revocation of conditions on approval",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "68 Notice before changes to conditions on approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-68"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator must not, on the Digital ID Regulator’s\nown initiative:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System after the approval has been given; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition imposed under subsection 66(1);\nunless the Digital ID Regulator has given the entity a written notice\nin accordance with subsection (2) of this section.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) state the proposed condition, variation or revocation; and\n(b) request the entity to give the Digital ID Regulator, within the\nperiod specified in the notice, a written statement relating to\nthe proposed condition, variation or revocation.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must consider any written statement\ngiven within the period specified in the notice before making a\ndecision to:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition under subsection 66(1) on an\nentity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government\nDigital ID System.\n(4) This section does not apply if the Digital ID Regulator reasonably\nbelieves that the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is\nserious and urgent.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 69\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(5) If this section does not apply to an entity because of subsection (4),\nthe Digital ID Regulator must give a written statement of reasons\nto the entity as to why the Digital ID Regulator reasonably believes\nthat the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is serious and\nurgent.\n(6) The statement of reasons under subsection (5) must be given within\n7 days after the condition is imposed, varied or revoked.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator must not, on the Digital ID Regulator’s\nown initiative:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System after the approval has been given; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition imposed under subsection 66(1);\nunless the Digital ID Regulator has given the entity a written notice\nin accordance with subsection (2) of this section.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) state the proposed condition, variation or revocation; and\n(b) request the entity to give the Digital ID Regulator, within the\nperiod specified in the notice, a written statement relating to\nthe proposed condition, variation or revocation.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must consider any written statement\ngiven within the period specified in the notice before making a\ndecision to:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition under subsection 66(1) on an\nentity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government\nDigital ID System.\n(4) This section does not apply if the Digital ID Regulator reasonably\nbelieves that the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is\nserious and urgent.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 69\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(5) If this section does not apply to an entity because of subsection (4),\nthe Digital ID Regulator must give a written statement of reasons\nto the entity as to why the Digital ID Regulator reasonably believes\nthat the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is serious and\nurgent.\n(6) The statement of reasons under subsection (5) must be given within\n7 days after the condition is imposed, varied or revoked.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-68-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "95940979628681ff7e7f2fab3e2b6664eb4a3f3b3ca4339b53ff2136da0ba394"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-68",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "68 Notice before changes to conditions on approval",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Regulator must not, on the Digital ID Regulator’s\nown initiative:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System after the approval has been given; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition imposed under subsection 66(1);\nunless the Digital ID Regulator has given the entity a written notice\nin accordance with subsection (2) of this section.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) state the proposed condition, variation or revocation; and\n(b) request the entity to give the Digital ID Regulator, within the\nperiod specified in the notice, a written statement relating to\nthe proposed condition, variation or revocation.\n(3) The Digital ID Regulator must consider any written statement\ngiven within the period specified in the notice before making a\ndecision to:\n(a) impose a condition under paragraph 64(2)(a) on an entity’s\napproval to participate in the Australian Government Digital\nID System; or\n(b) vary or revoke a condition under subsection 66(1) on an\nentity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government\nDigital ID System.\n(4) This section does not apply if the Digital ID Regulator reasonably\nbelieves that the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is\nserious and urgent.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nParticipating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2\nSection 69\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(5) If this section does not apply to an entity because of subsection (4),\nthe Digital ID Regulator must give a written statement of reasons\nto the entity as to why the Digital ID Regulator reasonably believes\nthat the need to impose, vary or revoke the condition is serious and\nurgent.\n(6) The statement of reasons under subsection (5) must be given within\n7 days after the condition is imposed, varied or revoked."
    },
