    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "69 Notice of decision of changes of conditions on approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-69"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an\nentity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a\ncondition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of\nthe decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under\nsubsection 62(5).\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition\nis revoked; and\n(b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation\ntakes effect.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an\nentity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a\ncondition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of\nthe decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under\nsubsection 62(5).\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition\nis revoked; and\n(b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation\ntakes effect.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e899eefd831dcc2c6876dde457f5437f6445468a944cf26bd02253634d4d34f5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-69",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69 Notice of decision of changes of conditions on approval",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an\nentity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a\ncondition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System.\n(2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of\nthe decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under\nsubsection 62(5).\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition\nis revoked; and\n(b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation\ntakes effect.\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System"
    },
