      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether the Digital ID Regulator is satisfied of the\nmatter in paragraph (2)(e), regard may be had to whether the entity\nis a fit and proper person.\nNote:\nIn having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person, the\nDigital ID Regulator must have regard to any matters specified in the\nDigital ID Rules and may have regard to any other matters considered\nrelevant (see section 12).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining whether the Digital ID Regulator is satisfied of the\nmatter in paragraph (2)(e), regard may be had to whether the entity\nis a fit and proper person.\nNote:\nIn having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person, the\nDigital ID Regulator must have regard to any matters specified in the\nDigital ID Rules and may have regard to any other matters considered\nrelevant (see section 12).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-71"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-71-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-71-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1543cf0ab8ceac9be763ab1b48beb002e7e26c10995509255f2c1b452b817175",
      "skos:note": "Consideration of an entity's fit and proper person status when determining approval to participate in the Australian Digital ID system."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-71-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "71(3) Suspension of approval to participate in the Australian",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining whether the Digital ID Regulator is satisfied of the\nmatter in paragraph (2)(e), regard may be had to whether the entity\nis a fit and proper person.\nNote:\nIn having regard to whether an entity is a fit and proper person, the\nDigital ID Regulator must have regard to any matters specified in the\nDigital ID Rules and may have regard to any other matters considered\nrelevant (see section 12)."
    },
