    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Minister’s directions regarding participation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to approve an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System;\n(b) impose conditions on the approval of an entity to participate\nin the Australian Government Digital ID System;\n(c) suspend the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System;\n(d) revoke the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 74\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to approve an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System;\n(b) impose conditions on the approval of an entity to participate\nin the Australian Government Digital ID System;\n(c) suspend the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System;\n(d) revoke the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 74\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-73-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd50b3eddc053ebab6a4129e9a42540c5c0f2d9367fe06d612357ddf22ad1281"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-73",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 Minister’s directions regarding participation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Digital ID Regulator to do\nany of the following if, for reasons of security (within the meaning\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979),\nincluding on the basis of an adverse or qualified security\nassessment in respect of a person, the Minister considers it\nappropriate to do so:\n(a) refuse to approve an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System;\n(b) impose conditions on the approval of an entity to participate\nin the Australian Government Digital ID System;\n(c) suspend the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System;\n(d) revoke the approval of an entity to participate in the\nAustralian Government Digital ID System.\n(2) If the Minister gives a direction under subsection (1), the Digital\nID Regulator must comply with the direction.\n(3) The direction remains in force unless it is revoked by the Minister.\nThe Minister must notify the Digital ID Regulator and the entity if\nthe Minister revokes the direction.\n(4) Despite subsection (3), a direction given under subsection (1) to\nrevoke the approval of an entity to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System cannot be revoked.\n(5) A direction given under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 74\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
