    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "74 Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-74"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.97",
      "values:originalText": "Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary\n(1) A participating relying party must not, as a condition of providing\na service or access to a service, require an individual to create or\nuse a digital ID.\nNote:\nThe effect of this subsection is that a participating relying party that\nprovides a service, or access to a service, must provide another means\nof accessing that service that does not involve the creation or use of a\ndigital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System.\n(1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1)\nif:\n(a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access\nto the service, by means other than the creation or use of a\ndigital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID\nSystem; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the other means is not reasonably accessible;\n(ii) using the other means results in the service being\nprovided on substantially less favourable terms.\nExceptions\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying\nparty if:\n(a) the service provides access to another service; and\n(b) the individual can access the other service by means other\nthan the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "skos:definition": "Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary\n(1) A participating relying party must not, as a condition of providing\na service or access to a service, require an individual to create or\nuse a digital ID.\nNote:\nThe effect of this subsection is that a participating relying party that\nprovides a service, or access to a service, must provide another means\nof accessing that service that does not involve the creation or use of a\ndigital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System.\n(1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1)\nif:\n(a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access\nto the service, by means other than the creation or use of a\ndigital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID\nSystem; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the other means is not reasonably accessible;\n(ii) using the other means results in the service being\nprovided on substantially less favourable terms.\nExceptions\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying\nparty if:\n(a) the service provides access to another service; and\n(b) the individual can access the other service by means other\nthan the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and\n\nChapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
