    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "81 Entities may conduct testing in the Australian Government",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-81"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "Digital ID System\n(1) The System Administrator may authorise an entity to conduct\ntesting in the Australian Government Digital ID System for the\npurposes of determining the entity’s capability or suitability to\nparticipate in the system.\n(2) The authorisation:\n(a) must be in writing; and\n(b) must specify the period for which it is in force, which must\nnot exceed 3 months; and\n(c) may be granted unconditionally or subject to conditions.\nNote:\nThe System Administrator may vary or revoke the authorisation: see\nsubsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(3) If an authorisation under this section is given subject to a condition\nand the condition is not met at a particular time, the authorisation\nceases to be in force at that time.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 82\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "Digital ID System\n(1) The System Administrator may authorise an entity to conduct\ntesting in the Australian Government Digital ID System for the\npurposes of determining the entity’s capability or suitability to\nparticipate in the system.\n(2) The authorisation:\n(a) must be in writing; and\n(b) must specify the period for which it is in force, which must\nnot exceed 3 months; and\n(c) may be granted unconditionally or subject to conditions.\nNote:\nThe System Administrator may vary or revoke the authorisation: see\nsubsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(3) If an authorisation under this section is given subject to a condition\nand the condition is not met at a particular time, the authorisation\nceases to be in force at that time.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 82\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e15f31649f30bfa568e27dcb8711a2a3eca46f23089d63058dec7f467694d48b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-81",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "81 Entities may conduct testing in the Australian Government",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "Digital ID System\n(1) The System Administrator may authorise an entity to conduct\ntesting in the Australian Government Digital ID System for the\npurposes of determining the entity’s capability or suitability to\nparticipate in the system.\n(2) The authorisation:\n(a) must be in writing; and\n(b) must specify the period for which it is in force, which must\nnot exceed 3 months; and\n(c) may be granted unconditionally or subject to conditions.\nNote:\nThe System Administrator may vary or revoke the authorisation: see\nsubsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(3) If an authorisation under this section is given subject to a condition\nand the condition is not met at a particular time, the authorisation\nceases to be in force at that time.\n\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4\nAustralian Government Digital ID System  Part 2\nOther matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5\nSection 82\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81-ss-1",
