    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "116 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-116"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "The Digital ID Rules may set out marks, symbols, logos or designs\n(called digital ID trustmarks) that may or must be used by\naccredited entities and participating relying parties.\nAn entity may be liable to a civil penalty if the entity:\n(a)\nuses a digital ID trustmark and the entity is not\nauthorised by the Digital ID Rules to do so; or\n(b)\nis required by the Digital ID Rules to display a digital ID\ntrustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID\nRules and the entity fails to comply with the\nrequirement.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must establish and maintain the Digital\nID Accredited Entities Register, which is a register of entities that\nare, or have been, accredited entities.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must also establish and maintain the\nAGDIS Register, which is a register of entities that are approved to\nparticipate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.\n\nChapter 8  Trustmarks and registers",
      "skos:definition": "The Digital ID Rules may set out marks, symbols, logos or designs\n(called digital ID trustmarks) that may or must be used by\naccredited entities and participating relying parties.\nAn entity may be liable to a civil penalty if the entity:\n(a)\nuses a digital ID trustmark and the entity is not\nauthorised by the Digital ID Rules to do so; or\n(b)\nis required by the Digital ID Rules to display a digital ID\ntrustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID\nRules and the entity fails to comply with the\nrequirement.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must establish and maintain the Digital\nID Accredited Entities Register, which is a register of entities that\nare, or have been, accredited entities.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must also establish and maintain the\nAGDIS Register, which is a register of entities that are approved to\nparticipate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.\n\nChapter 8  Trustmarks and registers",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2794c297c064991277abba37139d4eaf2490e5ef463089e13238a29745fbe01",
      "skos:note": "Using digital ID trustmark without authorization is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-116",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "116 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "The Digital ID Rules may set out marks, symbols, logos or designs\n(called digital ID trustmarks) that may or must be used by\naccredited entities and participating relying parties.\nAn entity may be liable to a civil penalty if the entity:\n(a)\nuses a digital ID trustmark and the entity is not\nauthorised by the Digital ID Rules to do so; or\n(b)\nis required by the Digital ID Rules to display a digital ID\ntrustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID\nRules and the entity fails to comply with the\nrequirement.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must establish and maintain the Digital\nID Accredited Entities Register, which is a register of entities that\nare, or have been, accredited entities.\nThe Digital ID Regulator must also establish and maintain the\nAGDIS Register, which is a register of entities that are approved to\nparticipate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.\n\nChapter 8  Trustmarks and registers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of unauthorized use",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity uses digital ID trustmark without authorization.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Entity is liable to civil penalty."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal relation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relation between entity's actions and penalties",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity is liable to civil penalty if the entity uses digital ID trustmark without authorization.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Penalty applies when entity uses unauthorized trustmark."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implication of failure to comply with requirements",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity fails to display digital ID trustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID Rules.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Entity is liable to civil penalty."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Propagation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Propagation of penalties through entity's actions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Entity uses digital ID trustmark without authorization.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Penalty applies when entity uses unauthorized trustmark."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-117",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "117 Digital ID trustmarks",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-117"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Rules may do one or more of the following:\n(a) specify one or more digital ID trustmarks that may or must\nbe used by accredited entities;\n(b) specify one or more digital ID trustmarks that may or must\nbe used by participating relying parties;\n(c) prescribe conditions or requirements in relation to the use or\ndisplay of those digital ID trustmarks.\n(2) Digital ID trustmark means a mark, symbol, logo or design set out\nin the Digital ID Rules.\n118  Authorised use of digital ID trustmarks etc.\n(1) An entity is authorised to use a digital ID trustmark if:\n(a) the Digital ID Rules permit or require the entity to use the\ndigital ID trustmark; and\n(b) if the Digital ID Rules prescribe conditions in relation to the\nuse or display of the digital ID trustmark—the entity\ncomplies with the conditions.\n(2) An entity must not use a digital ID trustmark if the entity is not\nauthorised under subsection (1) to use the trustmark.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n(3) An entity must not do any of the following in relation to a mark,\nsymbol, logo or design so closely resembling a digital ID trustmark\nas to be likely to lead a reasonable person to believe that the entity\nis an accredited entity or a participating relying party:\n(a) use it in relation to a business, trade, profession or\noccupation;\n\nTrustmarks and registers  Chapter 8\nDigital ID trustmarks  Part 2\n\nSection 119\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) apply (as a trade mark or otherwise) it to goods imported,\nmanufactured, produced, sold, offered for sale or let on hire;\n(c) use it in relation to:\n(i) goods or services; or\n(ii) the promotion (by any means) of the supply or use of\ngoods or services.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Digital ID Rules may do one or more of the following:\n(a) specify one or more digital ID trustmarks that may or must\nbe used by accredited entities;\n(b) specify one or more digital ID trustmarks that may or must\nbe used by participating relying parties;\n(c) prescribe conditions or requirements in relation to the use or\ndisplay of those digital ID trustmarks.\n(2) Digital ID trustmark means a mark, symbol, logo or design set out\nin the Digital ID Rules.\n118  Authorised use of digital ID trustmarks etc.\n(1) An entity is authorised to use a digital ID trustmark if:\n(a) the Digital ID Rules permit or require the entity to use the\ndigital ID trustmark; and\n(b) if the Digital ID Rules prescribe conditions in relation to the\nuse or display of the digital ID trustmark—the entity\ncomplies with the conditions.\n(2) An entity must not use a digital ID trustmark if the entity is not\nauthorised under subsection (1) to use the trustmark.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n(3) An entity must not do any of the following in relation to a mark,\nsymbol, logo or design so closely resembling a digital ID trustmark\nas to be likely to lead a reasonable person to believe that the entity\nis an accredited entity or a participating relying party:\n(a) use it in relation to a business, trade, profession or\noccupation;\n\nTrustmarks and registers  Chapter 8\nDigital ID trustmarks  Part 2\n\nSection 119\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) apply (as a trade mark or otherwise) it to goods imported,\nmanufactured, produced, sold, offered for sale or let on hire;\n(c) use it in relation to:\n(i) goods or services; or\n(ii) the promotion (by any means) of the supply or use of\ngoods or services.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-117-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-117-ss-2"
        },
        {
