      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) An entity must not use a digital ID trustmark if the entity is not authorized under subsection (1)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The class of entities that can use digital ID trustmarks includes those authorized under subsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-117-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "117(3) Digital ID trustmarks",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-117-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An entity must not do any of the following in relation to a mark,\nsymbol, logo or design so closely resembling a digital ID trustmark\nas to be likely to lead a reasonable person to believe that the entity\nis an accredited entity or a participating relying party:\n(a) use it in relation to a business, trade, profession or\noccupation;\n\nTrustmarks and registers  Chapter 8\nDigital ID trustmarks  Part 2\n\nSection 119\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) apply (as a trade mark or otherwise) it to goods imported,\nmanufactured, produced, sold, offered for sale or let on hire;\n(c) use it in relation to:\n(i) goods or services; or\n(ii) the promotion (by any means) of the supply or use of\ngoods or services.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An entity must not do any of the following in relation to a mark,\nsymbol, logo or design so closely resembling a digital ID trustmark\nas to be likely to lead a reasonable person to believe that the entity\nis an accredited entity or a participating relying party:\n(a) use it in relation to a business, trade, profession or\noccupation;\n\nTrustmarks and registers  Chapter 8\nDigital ID trustmarks  Part 2\n\nSection 119\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\n(b) apply (as a trade mark or otherwise) it to goods imported,\nmanufactured, produced, sold, offered for sale or let on hire;\n(c) use it in relation to:\n(i) goods or services; or\n(ii) the promotion (by any means) of the supply or use of\ngoods or services.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-117"
      },
