    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-130-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "130(2) System Administrator’s power to give directions to protect the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-130-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the System Administrator may\ngive a direction to do one or more of the following:\n(a) take or not take specified action in relation to the\nperformance of the Australian Government Digital ID\nSystem;\n(b) conduct a fraud assessment in relation to a specified matter\nand provide a copy of the report to the System Administrator\nin relation to the assessment;\n(c) conduct a security assessment in relation to a specified matter\nand provide a copy of the report to the System Administrator\nin relation to the assessment;\n(d) an act or thing specified by the Digital ID Rules.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the System Administrator may\ngive a direction to do one or more of the following:\n(a) take or not take specified action in relation to the\nperformance of the Australian Government Digital ID\nSystem;\n(b) conduct a fraud assessment in relation to a specified matter\nand provide a copy of the report to the System Administrator\nin relation to the assessment;\n(c) conduct a security assessment in relation to a specified matter\nand provide a copy of the report to the System Administrator\nin relation to the assessment;\n(d) an act or thing specified by the Digital ID Rules.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-130"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
