    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-135",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135 Record keeping by participating entities and former",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-135"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.151",
      "values:originalText": "participating entities\n(1) This section applies to:\n(a) entities that hold an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is suspended; and\n(c) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System has been revoked.\n(2) However, this section does not apply to relying parties.\n(3) The entity must keep records of the kind, for the period and in the\nmanner prescribed by the Digital ID Rules.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n(4) Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of subsection (3):\n(a) must not prescribe records of a kind that do not relate to\ninformation obtained by entities through the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) may only prescribe a period of retention of more than 7 years\nif specified circumstances apply in relation to the record.\nNote:\nFor the purposes of paragraph (b), specified circumstances may\ninclude legal proceedings involving the entity and the records.",
      "skos:definition": "participating entities\n(1) This section applies to:\n(a) entities that hold an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is suspended; and\n(c) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System has been revoked.\n(2) However, this section does not apply to relying parties.\n(3) The entity must keep records of the kind, for the period and in the\nmanner prescribed by the Digital ID Rules.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n(4) Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of subsection (3):\n(a) must not prescribe records of a kind that do not relate to\ninformation obtained by entities through the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) may only prescribe a period of retention of more than 7 years\nif specified circumstances apply in relation to the record.\nNote:\nFor the purposes of paragraph (b), specified circumstances may\ninclude legal proceedings involving the entity and the records.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-135-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-135-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-135-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-135-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a62692a10a050b147d096da3fcfe44c905b5fac4a697dac86137caccd91893ea"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-135",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135 Record keeping by participating entities and former",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 151,
      "values:originalText": "participating entities\n(1) This section applies to:\n(a) entities that hold an approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System is suspended; and\n(c) entities whose approval to participate in the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System has been revoked.\n(2) However, this section does not apply to relying parties.\n(3) The entity must keep records of the kind, for the period and in the\nmanner prescribed by the Digital ID Rules.\nCivil penalty:\n1,000 penalty units.\n(4) Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of subsection (3):\n(a) must not prescribe records of a kind that do not relate to\ninformation obtained by entities through the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System; and\n(b) may only prescribe a period of retention of more than 7 years\nif specified circumstances apply in relation to the record.\nNote:\nFor the purposes of paragraph (b), specified circumstances may\ninclude legal proceedings involving the entity and the records."
    },
