    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137 Reviewable decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-137"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A decision referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table\nis a reviewable decision. An entity referred to in column 2 of the\nitem is the affected entity for the decision.\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nColumn 1\nReviewable decision\nColumn 2\nAffected entity\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder section 15 to refuse to accredit\nan entity as an accredited entity (other\nthan on the ground referred to in\nparagraph 15(4)(a))\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder paragraph 17(2)(a) to impose a\ncondition on an entity’s accreditation\nThe entity on whom the condition\nis imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 17(2) to refuse to\nimpose, on application by an entity, a\ncondition on the entity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to vary, on the\nDigital ID Regulator’s own initiative,\nthe conditions imposed on an entity’s\naccreditation\nThe entity on whom the\nconditions are imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to refuse to\nvary, on application by an accredited\nentity, the conditions imposed on the\nentity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 25(2) to suspend the\nThe accredited entity\n\nChapter 9  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A decision referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table\nis a reviewable decision. An entity referred to in column 2 of the\nitem is the affected entity for the decision.\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nColumn 1\nReviewable decision\nColumn 2\nAffected entity\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder section 15 to refuse to accredit\nan entity as an accredited entity (other\nthan on the ground referred to in\nparagraph 15(4)(a))\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder paragraph 17(2)(a) to impose a\ncondition on an entity’s accreditation\nThe entity on whom the condition\nis imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 17(2) to refuse to\nimpose, on application by an entity, a\ncondition on the entity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to vary, on the\nDigital ID Regulator’s own initiative,\nthe conditions imposed on an entity’s\naccreditation\nThe entity on whom the\nconditions are imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to refuse to\nvary, on application by an accredited\nentity, the conditions imposed on the\nentity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 25(2) to suspend the\nThe accredited entity\n\nChapter 9  Administration",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "54170077b5fe315f5145f717c97b7e616e7ee681459e34409bd931c3ee40d106",
      "skos:note": "A decision by the Digital ID Regulator is a reviewable decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-137",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137 Reviewable decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A decision referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table\nis a reviewable decision. An entity referred to in column 2 of the\nitem is the affected entity for the decision.\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nColumn 1\nReviewable decision\nColumn 2\nAffected entity\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder section 15 to refuse to accredit\nan entity as an accredited entity (other\nthan on the ground referred to in\nparagraph 15(4)(a))\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder paragraph 17(2)(a) to impose a\ncondition on an entity’s accreditation\nThe entity on whom the condition\nis imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 17(2) to refuse to\nimpose, on application by an entity, a\ncondition on the entity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to vary, on the\nDigital ID Regulator’s own initiative,\nthe conditions imposed on an entity’s\naccreditation\nThe entity on whom the\nconditions are imposed\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 20(1) to refuse to\nvary, on application by an accredited\nentity, the conditions imposed on the\nentity’s accreditation\nThe entity who made the\napplication\nA decision by the Digital ID Regulator\nunder subsection 25(2) to suspend the\nThe accredited entity\n\nChapter 9  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The decision is an obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Digital ID Regulator has the power to make decisions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The decision is a reviewable decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The decision must occur during the accreditation process.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The accreditation process begins when an entity applies for accreditation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The decision must occur during the accreditation process."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If the Digital ID Regulator refuses to accredit an entity, then the entity is not accredited.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Digital ID Regulator has the power to refuse accreditation.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If the Digital ID Regulator refuses to accredit an entity, then the entity is not accredited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "if-and-only-if",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The decision can only be made if the entity has applied for accreditation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The entity must apply for accreditation before the Digital ID Regulator can make a decision.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The decision can only be made if the entity has applied for accreditation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is-a",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The decision is a type of artificial intelligence decision.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Digital ID Regulator uses artificial intelligence to make decisions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The decision is a type of artificial intelligence decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-138",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "138 Internal review of decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-138"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a reviewable decision is made by a delegate of the\ndecision-maker for the reviewable decision, the affected entity for\nthe reviewable decision may apply in writing to the decision-maker\nfor review (an internal review) of the decision.\n(2) An application for an internal review must be made within 28 days\nafter the day on which the decision first came to the notice of the\napplicant.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 9\nReview of decisions  Part 4\n\nSection 139\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a reviewable decision is made by a delegate of the\ndecision-maker for the reviewable decision, the affected entity for\nthe reviewable decision may apply in writing to the decision-maker\nfor review (an internal review) of the decision.\n(2) An application for an internal review must be made within 28 days\nafter the day on which the decision first came to the notice of the\napplicant.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 9\nReview of decisions  Part 4\n\nSection 139\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-138-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-138-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48a93249653f6d6b0628d1b23eee7e6be55a5a2a8c3f676a65a7beb7398700f2"
