    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-139",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139 Reconsideration by decision-maker",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-139"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.157",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 90 days after receiving an application under section 138 for\ninternal review, the decision-maker for the reviewable decision\nmust:\n(a) review the decision; and\n(b) affirm, vary or revoke the decision; and\n(c) if the decision-maker revokes the decision—make such other\ndecision (if any) that the decision-maker thinks appropriate.\n(2) The decision-maker for the reviewable decision must, as soon as\npracticable after making a decision under subsection (1), give the\napplicant a written statement of the decision-maker’s reasons for\nthe decision.\n(3) If the decision-maker’s functions under this section are performed\nby a delegate of the decision-maker for the reviewable decision,\nthe delegate who makes the decision under subsection (1):\n(a) must not have been involved in making the original\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) must hold a position or perform duties of a higher level than\nthe delegate who made the original reviewable decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Within 90 days after receiving an application under section 138 for\ninternal review, the decision-maker for the reviewable decision\nmust:\n(a) review the decision; and\n(b) affirm, vary or revoke the decision; and\n(c) if the decision-maker revokes the decision—make such other\ndecision (if any) that the decision-maker thinks appropriate.\n(2) The decision-maker for the reviewable decision must, as soon as\npracticable after making a decision under subsection (1), give the\napplicant a written statement of the decision-maker’s reasons for\nthe decision.\n(3) If the decision-maker’s functions under this section are performed\nby a delegate of the decision-maker for the reviewable decision,\nthe delegate who makes the decision under subsection (1):\n(a) must not have been involved in making the original\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) must hold a position or perform duties of a higher level than\nthe delegate who made the original reviewable decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-139-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-139-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-139-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9ade095b8828d033c7f907f7c895689307657071d1333ccbdb0ff9c81d030cf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-139",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139 Reconsideration by decision-maker",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 157,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 90 days after receiving an application under section 138 for\ninternal review, the decision-maker for the reviewable decision\nmust:\n(a) review the decision; and\n(b) affirm, vary or revoke the decision; and\n(c) if the decision-maker revokes the decision—make such other\ndecision (if any) that the decision-maker thinks appropriate.\n(2) The decision-maker for the reviewable decision must, as soon as\npracticable after making a decision under subsection (1), give the\napplicant a written statement of the decision-maker’s reasons for\nthe decision.\n(3) If the decision-maker’s functions under this section are performed\nby a delegate of the decision-maker for the reviewable decision,\nthe delegate who makes the decision under subsection (1):\n(a) must not have been involved in making the original\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) must hold a position or perform duties of a higher level than\nthe delegate who made the original reviewable decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-139-ss-1",
