    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-141",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "141 Requirements for applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-141"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application made under this Act must:\n(a) be given in a form and manner for that kind of application\napproved by the person to whom the application is made; and\n(b) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the form; and\n(c) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the Digital ID Rules or the Accreditation Rules; and\n(d) if Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144\nspecify a fee that must accompany the application and\npayment of the fee has not been waived—be accompanied by\nthe fee.\nNote:\nA decision on an application is not required to be made if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\n(2) The person to whom the application is made may accept any\ninformation or document previously given to the person in\nconnection with another application made under this Act as\nsatisfying any requirement to give that information or document\nunder subsection (1).\n(3) To avoid doubt, approval may be given for:\n(a) different forms for different kinds of applications; or\n(b) a single form for more than one kind of application.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application made under this Act must:\n(a) be given in a form and manner for that kind of application\napproved by the person to whom the application is made; and\n(b) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the form; and\n(c) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the Digital ID Rules or the Accreditation Rules; and\n(d) if Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144\nspecify a fee that must accompany the application and\npayment of the fee has not been waived—be accompanied by\nthe fee.\nNote:\nA decision on an application is not required to be made if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\n(2) The person to whom the application is made may accept any\ninformation or document previously given to the person in\nconnection with another application made under this Act as\nsatisfying any requirement to give that information or document\nunder subsection (1).\n(3) To avoid doubt, approval may be given for:\n(a) different forms for different kinds of applications; or\n(b) a single form for more than one kind of application.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-141-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-141-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-141-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "075d5f3b4c5b7ea57752713e2181858bd4b5a16bb9acb9226cb2608bc28cec0b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-141",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "141 Requirements for applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application made under this Act must:\n(a) be given in a form and manner for that kind of application\napproved by the person to whom the application is made; and\n(b) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the form; and\n(c) be accompanied by any information or documents required\nby the Digital ID Rules or the Accreditation Rules; and\n(d) if Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144\nspecify a fee that must accompany the application and\npayment of the fee has not been waived—be accompanied by\nthe fee.\nNote:\nA decision on an application is not required to be made if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\n(2) The person to whom the application is made may accept any\ninformation or document previously given to the person in\nconnection with another application made under this Act as\nsatisfying any requirement to give that information or document\nunder subsection (1).\n(3) To avoid doubt, approval may be given for:\n(a) different forms for different kinds of applications; or\n(b) a single form for more than one kind of application."
    },
