    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-142",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "142 Powers in relation to applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-142"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person (the applicant) makes an application under this Act, the\nperson to whom the application is made may, by written notice,\nrequire the applicant to give the person such further information or\ndocuments in relation to the application as the person reasonably\nrequires.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 9\nApplications under this Act  Part 5\n\nSection 143\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote 1:\nThe person is not required to make a decision on the application if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\nNote 2:\nThe Digital ID Regulator may also require an applicant to undergo a\ncompliance assessment before making a decision on the application\n(see section 131).\n(2) A notice under subsection (1) may specify a period, which must\nnot be less than 14 days, within which the information or\ndocuments must be given.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person (the applicant) makes an application under this Act, the\nperson to whom the application is made may, by written notice,\nrequire the applicant to give the person such further information or\ndocuments in relation to the application as the person reasonably\nrequires.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 9\nApplications under this Act  Part 5\n\nSection 143\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote 1:\nThe person is not required to make a decision on the application if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\nNote 2:\nThe Digital ID Regulator may also require an applicant to undergo a\ncompliance assessment before making a decision on the application\n(see section 131).\n(2) A notice under subsection (1) may specify a period, which must\nnot be less than 14 days, within which the information or\ndocuments must be given.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-142-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-142-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4c47a9c6decda20766d9d86d9c29b1c68e8356defbd8e1e2f26ba5ca2fce008e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-142",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "142 Powers in relation to applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person (the applicant) makes an application under this Act, the\nperson to whom the application is made may, by written notice,\nrequire the applicant to give the person such further information or\ndocuments in relation to the application as the person reasonably\nrequires.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 9\nApplications under this Act  Part 5\n\nSection 143\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nNote 1:\nThe person is not required to make a decision on the application if this\nsubsection is not complied with (see section 143).\nNote 2:\nThe Digital ID Regulator may also require an applicant to undergo a\ncompliance assessment before making a decision on the application\n(see section 131).\n(2) A notice under subsection (1) may specify a period, which must\nnot be less than 14 days, within which the information or\ndocuments must be given."
    },
