    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "143 Decisions not required to be made in certain circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-143"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.159",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If this Act requires an application to be in a form approved by the\nperson to whom the application is made, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application if it is not in that form.\n(2) If this Act requires an application to be accompanied by\ninformation or documents, the person to whom the application is\nmade is not required to make a decision on the application until the\ninformation or documents are provided.\n(3) If this Act permits a person to require further information or\ndocuments in relation to an application, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application until the information or\ndocuments are provided.\n(4) If the Digital ID Regulator requires a compliance assessment to be\nconducted for the purposes of making a decision under this Act, the\nDigital ID Regulator is not required to make the decision until the\nassessment is conducted.\n(5) If Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144 specify a\nfee that must accompany an application and payment of the fee has\nnot been waived, the person to whom the application is made is not\nrequired to make a decision on the application until the fee is paid.\n\nChapter 9  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If this Act requires an application to be in a form approved by the\nperson to whom the application is made, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application if it is not in that form.\n(2) If this Act requires an application to be accompanied by\ninformation or documents, the person to whom the application is\nmade is not required to make a decision on the application until the\ninformation or documents are provided.\n(3) If this Act permits a person to require further information or\ndocuments in relation to an application, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application until the information or\ndocuments are provided.\n(4) If the Digital ID Regulator requires a compliance assessment to be\nconducted for the purposes of making a decision under this Act, the\nDigital ID Regulator is not required to make the decision until the\nassessment is conducted.\n(5) If Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144 specify a\nfee that must accompany an application and payment of the fee has\nnot been waived, the person to whom the application is made is not\nrequired to make a decision on the application until the fee is paid.\n\nChapter 9  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1e2ea11292b4b9836c1cc97652bcbadb69475790f7f430821fddefdc850d721"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-143",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "143 Decisions not required to be made in certain circumstances",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If this Act requires an application to be in a form approved by the\nperson to whom the application is made, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application if it is not in that form.\n(2) If this Act requires an application to be accompanied by\ninformation or documents, the person to whom the application is\nmade is not required to make a decision on the application until the\ninformation or documents are provided.\n(3) If this Act permits a person to require further information or\ndocuments in relation to an application, the person is not required\nto make a decision on the application until the information or\ndocuments are provided.\n(4) If the Digital ID Regulator requires a compliance assessment to be\nconducted for the purposes of making a decision under this Act, the\nDigital ID Regulator is not required to make the decision until the\nassessment is conducted.\n(5) If Digital ID Rules made for the purposes of section 144 specify a\nfee that must accompany an application and payment of the fee has\nnot been waived, the person to whom the application is made is not\nrequired to make a decision on the application until the fee is paid.\n\nChapter 9  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-143-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
