    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-148-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "148(3) Charging of fees by accredited entities in relation to the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-148-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Digital ID Rules may do any\nof the following:\n(a) prescribe a fee by specifying the amount of the fee or a\nmethod of working out the fee;\n(b) make provision for when and how fees may be charged;\n(c) make provision in relation to the conduct of periodic reviews\nof fees;\n(d) make provision for any other matters in relation to the\ncharging of fees, including in relation to exemptions, refunds,\nremissions or waivers.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Digital ID Rules may do any\nof the following:\n(a) prescribe a fee by specifying the amount of the fee or a\nmethod of working out the fee;\n(b) make provision for when and how fees may be charged;\n(c) make provision in relation to the conduct of periodic reviews\nof fees;\n(d) make provision for any other matters in relation to the\ncharging of fees, including in relation to exemptions, refunds,\nremissions or waivers.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-148"
      },
