    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "149 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-149"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may establish advisory committees to provide advice\nto the following in relation to matters arising under this Act:\n(a)\nthe Minister;\n(b)\nthe Secretary;\n(c)\nthe Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\nA person commits an offence if the person obtains certain kinds of\ninformation in the course of, or for the purposes of, performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under this Act and the person uses\nor discloses the information. There are some exceptions.\nThis Chapter also deals with matters of an administrative nature,\nincluding:\n(a)\nannual reports by the Digital ID Regulator, the\nInformation Commissioner, law enforcement agencies,\nenforcement bodies and the AFP Minister; and\n(b)\ndelegations; and\n(c)\nrule-making powers.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nAdvisory committees  Part 2\n\nSection 150\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "The Minister may establish advisory committees to provide advice\nto the following in relation to matters arising under this Act:\n(a)\nthe Minister;\n(b)\nthe Secretary;\n(c)\nthe Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\nA person commits an offence if the person obtains certain kinds of\ninformation in the course of, or for the purposes of, performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under this Act and the person uses\nor discloses the information. There are some exceptions.\nThis Chapter also deals with matters of an administrative nature,\nincluding:\n(a)\nannual reports by the Digital ID Regulator, the\nInformation Commissioner, law enforcement agencies,\nenforcement bodies and the AFP Minister; and\n(b)\ndelegations; and\n(c)\nrule-making powers.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nAdvisory committees  Part 2\n\nSection 150\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b186eec0e4d8d5aef41506479bf33f7782d2da9dff4a1b0f79d78796494c2042",
      "skos:note": "Minister may establish advisory committees."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-149",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "149 Simplified outline of this Chapter",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "The Minister may establish advisory committees to provide advice\nto the following in relation to matters arising under this Act:\n(a)\nthe Minister;\n(b)\nthe Secretary;\n(c)\nthe Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\nA person commits an offence if the person obtains certain kinds of\ninformation in the course of, or for the purposes of, performing\nfunctions or exercising powers under this Act and the person uses\nor discloses the information. There are some exceptions.\nThis Chapter also deals with matters of an administrative nature,\nincluding:\n(a)\nannual reports by the Digital ID Regulator, the\nInformation Commissioner, law enforcement agencies,\nenforcement bodies and the AFP Minister; and\n(b)\ndelegations; and\n(c)\nrule-making powers.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nAdvisory committees  Part 2\n\nSection 150\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-149-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "establish",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishing advisory committees is an obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-150",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "150 Advisory committees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-150"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.165",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may establish, in writing, such advisory committees\nas the Minister considers appropriate to provide advice to the\nfollowing in relation to matters arising under this Act, including\nbut not limited to the performance of the Digital ID Regulator’s\nfunctions and exercise of the Digital ID Regulator’s powers under\nthis Act:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) the System Administrator;\n(d) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\n(2) An advisory committee is to consist of such persons as the Minister\ndetermines.\n(3) If the Minister establishes an advisory committee under\nsubsection (1), the Minister must, in writing, determine:\n(a) the committee’s terms of reference; and\n(b) the terms and conditions of appointment of the members of\nthe committee, including:\n(i) term of office; and\n(ii) remuneration; and\n(iii) allowances; and\n(iv) leave of absence; and\n(v) disclosure of interests; and\n(vi) termination of membership; and\n(c) the procedures to be followed by the committee.\n(4) An instrument made under subsection (1) or (3) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may establish, in writing, such advisory committees\nas the Minister considers appropriate to provide advice to the\nfollowing in relation to matters arising under this Act, including\nbut not limited to the performance of the Digital ID Regulator’s\nfunctions and exercise of the Digital ID Regulator’s powers under\nthis Act:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) the System Administrator;\n(d) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\n(2) An advisory committee is to consist of such persons as the Minister\ndetermines.\n(3) If the Minister establishes an advisory committee under\nsubsection (1), the Minister must, in writing, determine:\n(a) the committee’s terms of reference; and\n(b) the terms and conditions of appointment of the members of\nthe committee, including:\n(i) term of office; and\n(ii) remuneration; and\n(iii) allowances; and\n(iv) leave of absence; and\n(v) disclosure of interests; and\n(vi) termination of membership; and\n(c) the procedures to be followed by the committee.\n(4) An instrument made under subsection (1) or (3) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-150-ss-1"
