      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-153",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153 Disclosing personal or commercially sensitive information to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-153"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "courts and tribunals etc. by entrusted persons\n(1) Except where it is necessary to do so for the purposes of giving\neffect to this Act, an entrusted person is not to be required:\n(a) to produce a document containing protected information to a\nbody mentioned in subsection (2); or\n(b) to disclose protected information to such a body;\nif either of the following applies:\n(c) the information is personal information of an individual other\nthan the entrusted person;\n(d) there is a risk that production of the document or disclosure\nof the information might substantially prejudice the\ncommercial interests of a person.\n(2) The bodies are a court, tribunal, authority or other person having\npower to require the production of documents or the answering of\nquestions.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 154\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "courts and tribunals etc. by entrusted persons\n(1) Except where it is necessary to do so for the purposes of giving\neffect to this Act, an entrusted person is not to be required:\n(a) to produce a document containing protected information to a\nbody mentioned in subsection (2); or\n(b) to disclose protected information to such a body;\nif either of the following applies:\n(c) the information is personal information of an individual other\nthan the entrusted person;\n(d) there is a risk that production of the document or disclosure\nof the information might substantially prejudice the\ncommercial interests of a person.\n(2) The bodies are a court, tribunal, authority or other person having\npower to require the production of documents or the answering of\nquestions.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 154\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-153-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-153-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "535a571f73640ec42773e554ed50ed2d2ba2d779cd58e1805b28e6333d7ed2c9"
    },
