    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154 Annual report by the Digital ID Regulator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-154"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must\nprepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the\nParliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the\nfinancial year.\n(2) The report must include the following:\n(a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme,\nincluding:\n(i) the number of applications for accreditation made under\nsection 14; and\n(ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15;\n(b) information about the operation of the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System, including:\n(i) the number of applications made to participate in the\nsystem under section 61; and\n(ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the\nsystem under section 62; and\n(iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber\nsecurity incidents, and the responses to any such\nincidents;\n(c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to\nthe Digital ID Regulator.\n(3) The report must be given to the Minister by:\n(a) the 30th day of October; or\n(b) the end of any further period granted under\nsubsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must\nprepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the\nParliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the\nfinancial year.\n(2) The report must include the following:\n(a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme,\nincluding:\n(i) the number of applications for accreditation made under\nsection 14; and\n(ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15;\n(b) information about the operation of the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System, including:\n(i) the number of applications made to participate in the\nsystem under section 61; and\n(ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the\nsystem under section 62; and\n(iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber\nsecurity incidents, and the responses to any such\nincidents;\n(c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to\nthe Digital ID Regulator.\n(3) The report must be given to the Minister by:\n(a) the 30th day of October; or\n(b) the end of any further period granted under\nsubsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e682a1da4c515fa8ddcbcc55b307fd90fc2bec5dcea6bd50040810b995b7b59d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-154",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154 Annual report by the Digital ID Regulator",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must\nprepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the\nParliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the\nfinancial year.\n(2) The report must include the following:\n(a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme,\nincluding:\n(i) the number of applications for accreditation made under\nsection 14; and\n(ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15;\n(b) information about the operation of the Australian\nGovernment Digital ID System, including:\n(i) the number of applications made to participate in the\nsystem under section 61; and\n(ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the\nsystem under section 62; and\n(iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber\nsecurity incidents, and the responses to any such\nincidents;\n(c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to\nthe Digital ID Regulator.\n(3) The report must be given to the Minister by:\n(a) the 30th day of October; or\n(b) the end of any further period granted under\nsubsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154(1) Annual report by the Digital ID Regulator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-154-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
