    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-155b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155B Annual report by AFP Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-155b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.171",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The AFP Minister must prepare a report in relation to the provision\nof reports (section 155A reports) under section 155A for a\nfinancial year.\n(2) If no section 155A reports were provided for the financial year, the\nreport by the AFP Minister must include a statement to that effect.\n(3) If subsection (2) does not apply, the report by the AFP Minister\nmust include the following in relation to each law enforcement\nagency and enforcement body that provided a section 155A report\nfor the financial year:\n(a) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body during the financial\nyear;\n(b) details of the type of information requested or required (but\nnot including personal information of a particular individual\nor details that would identify a particular individual) by the\nlaw enforcement agency or enforcement body during the\nfinancial year;\n(c) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body that were complied\nwith (in whole or in part) by an accredited entity during the\nfinancial year.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The AFP Minister must prepare a report in relation to the provision\nof reports (section 155A reports) under section 155A for a\nfinancial year.\n(2) If no section 155A reports were provided for the financial year, the\nreport by the AFP Minister must include a statement to that effect.\n(3) If subsection (2) does not apply, the report by the AFP Minister\nmust include the following in relation to each law enforcement\nagency and enforcement body that provided a section 155A report\nfor the financial year:\n(a) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body during the financial\nyear;\n(b) details of the type of information requested or required (but\nnot including personal information of a particular individual\nor details that would identify a particular individual) by the\nlaw enforcement agency or enforcement body during the\nfinancial year;\n(c) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body that were complied\nwith (in whole or in part) by an accredited entity during the\nfinancial year.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-155b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-155b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-155b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "020fafe07e0b58679234dfc2473c3a7807a61250efd57d0f5bb61deb4a091870"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-155b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155B Annual report by AFP Minister",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 171,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The AFP Minister must prepare a report in relation to the provision\nof reports (section 155A reports) under section 155A for a\nfinancial year.\n(2) If no section 155A reports were provided for the financial year, the\nreport by the AFP Minister must include a statement to that effect.\n(3) If subsection (2) does not apply, the report by the AFP Minister\nmust include the following in relation to each law enforcement\nagency and enforcement body that provided a section 155A report\nfor the financial year:\n(a) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body during the financial\nyear;\n(b) details of the type of information requested or required (but\nnot including personal information of a particular individual\nor details that would identify a particular individual) by the\nlaw enforcement agency or enforcement body during the\nfinancial year;\n(c) the total number of requests or requirements made by the law\nenforcement agency or enforcement body that were complied\nwith (in whole or in part) by an accredited entity during the\nfinancial year.\n\nChapter 10  Other matters"
    },
