      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Determine whether Commonwealth, State or Territory has contravened the Act",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158 Bodies corporate and due diligence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-158"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (about\nattributing contraventions of employees etc. to a body corporate), a\nbody corporate does not contravene a civil penalty provision of this\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 159\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nAct because of conduct of a person that the body corporate is taken\nto have engaged in, if it is established that the body corporate took\nreasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the\nconduct.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (about\nattributing contraventions of employees etc. to a body corporate), a\nbody corporate does not contravene a civil penalty provision of this\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 159\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nAct because of conduct of a person that the body corporate is taken\nto have engaged in, if it is established that the body corporate took\nreasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the\nconduct.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa71aabfccb9e6261056611573b3a63390a6c71c660df22b6708310ff9bcf66b",
      "skos:note": "Due diligence obligation for bodies corporate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-158",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158 Bodies corporate and due diligence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of section 97 of the Regulatory Powers Act (about\nattributing contraventions of employees etc. to a body corporate), a\nbody corporate does not contravene a civil penalty provision of this\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 159\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025\nAct because of conduct of a person that the body corporate is taken\nto have engaged in, if it is established that the body corporate took\nreasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the\nconduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-158-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to exercise due diligence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Bodies corporate must take reasonable precautions and exercise due diligence",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No contravention if due diligence is exercised"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-159",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "159 Protection from civil action",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-159"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.175",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(c) a member of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010);\n(d) an associate member of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(e) a member of the staff of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(f) the System Administrator;\n(g) a person referred to in section 16 of the Human Services\n(Centrelink) Act 1997;\n(h) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair;\n(i) the staff referred to in section 115 of this Act.\n(2) A person mentioned in subsection (1) is not liable to an action or\nother proceeding for damages for, or in relation to, an act done or\nomitted to be done in good faith by the person:\n(a) in the performance, or purported performance, of any\nfunctions under this Act; or\n(b) in the exercise, or purported exercise, of any powers under\nthis Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(c) a member of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010);\n(d) an associate member of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(e) a member of the staff of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(f) the System Administrator;\n(g) a person referred to in section 16 of the Human Services\n(Centrelink) Act 1997;\n(h) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair;\n(i) the staff referred to in section 115 of this Act.\n(2) A person mentioned in subsection (1) is not liable to an action or\nother proceeding for damages for, or in relation to, an act done or\nomitted to be done in good faith by the person:\n(a) in the performance, or purported performance, of any\nfunctions under this Act; or\n(b) in the exercise, or purported exercise, of any powers under\nthis Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-159-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-159-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee3144ab3406a9722f3f77ecbf107f311eccdb687b3a866c3e2d64c41234aa73"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-159",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "159 Protection from civil action",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 175,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(c) a member of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010);\n(d) an associate member of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(e) a member of the staff of the Australian Competition and\nConsumer Commission;\n(f) the System Administrator;\n(g) a person referred to in section 16 of the Human Services\n(Centrelink) Act 1997;\n(h) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair;\n(i) the staff referred to in section 115 of this Act.\n(2) A person mentioned in subsection (1) is not liable to an action or\nother proceeding for damages for, or in relation to, an act done or\nomitted to be done in good faith by the person:\n(a) in the performance, or purported performance, of any\nfunctions under this Act; or\n(b) in the exercise, or purported exercise, of any powers under\nthis Act."
    },
