    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-163",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "163 Delegation—Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-163"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.179",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate all or any of the Minister’s\nfunctions or powers under this Act (other than the Minister’s power\nunder section 168) to any of the following:\n(a) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) an SES employee or acting SES employee in the Department.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising powers or performing functions under the delegation,\nthe delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nMinister.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate all or any of the Minister’s\nfunctions or powers under this Act (other than the Minister’s power\nunder section 168) to any of the following:\n(a) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) an SES employee or acting SES employee in the Department.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising powers or performing functions under the delegation,\nthe delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nMinister.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-163-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-163-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "81ca791be06a25f70e0a72afee0588bd8c8effefe9e2b36ee635429eab606f5d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-163",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "163 Delegation—Minister",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 179,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate all or any of the Minister’s\nfunctions or powers under this Act (other than the Minister’s power\nunder section 168) to any of the following:\n(a) the Digital ID Regulator;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) an SES employee or acting SES employee in the Department.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising powers or performing functions under the delegation,\nthe delegate must comply with any written directions of the\nMinister."
    },
