      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of delegation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-166",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166 Delegation—Digital ID Data Standards Chair",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-166"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.180",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any\nor all of the Chair’s functions or powers under this Act to a person\nassisting the Chair under section 115 who is:\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee; or\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nsection 99 (about making Digital ID Data Standards).\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 167\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Digital ID Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any\nor all of the Chair’s functions or powers under this Act to a person\nassisting the Chair under section 115 who is:\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee; or\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nsection 99 (about making Digital ID Data Standards).\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 167\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-166-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-166-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-166-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e763b51631ede506126e392cd567bc07957d0fbccc776fc31957514e168e8705"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/digital-id-act-2024#sec-166",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166 Delegation—Digital ID Data Standards Chair",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 180,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Digital ID Data Standards Chair may delegate, in writing, any\nor all of the Chair’s functions or powers under this Act to a person\nassisting the Chair under section 115 who is:\n(a) an SES employee, or an acting SES employee; or\n(b) an APS employee who is holding or performing the duties of\na specified office or position that the Chair is satisfied is\nsufficiently senior for the APS employee to perform the\nfunction or exercise the power.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the function referred to in\nsection 99 (about making Digital ID Data Standards).\n(3) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the delegate under subsection (1) must comply with any\ndirections of the Digital ID Data Standards Chair.\n\nOther matters  Chapter 10\nOther matters  Part 4\n\nSection 167\nDigital ID Act 2024\nCompilation date: 21/02/2025"
    },
    {
